  "body": "Found during #2720 (PR #2735). The 2D Adaptive generator with `optimal_load` 0.5 did not finish in 9 minutes in a debug build. The same op at the seed `optimal_load` finished in about 170 s. I did not test a release build. Thus this can be a slow generator and not a hang.\n\n## Reproduction\n\n- Machine: `assets/machines/tormach-770mx-microarc4.mch` (`LoadMachine::from_file`).\n- Tool: catalog `EM-0600-4FL` (6 mm end mill).\n- Part: `geometry::cube((5, -15, -15), (35, 15, 15))`, imported with `ImportModel::from_mesh(\"part\", ...)`.\n- Stock: `StockShape::Box { dx: 40, dy: 50, dz: 50 }` at `Location { pos: (20, 0, -25), rot: IDENTITY_Q }`. The stock is [0, 40] x [-25, 25] x [-25, 25].\n- Operation: `seed_params(OpType::Adaptive2D.ordinal())`, source `SrcRef::Entity(\"part\")`, then:\n  - `top_z` 16, `bottom_z` 12, `stepdown` 4, `stepover` 3 (all `Height::fixed`);\n  - `clearance_z` 40, `retract_z` None;\n  - `optimal_load` 0.5 (the other fields are the seed values);\n  - area controls `AreaControls { offset: 3.0, ..Default::default() }` through `EditOperationParams::with_area`.\n- Tilt: the test ran three poses in sequence in one test: upright (no tilt), then `Tilt { basis_version: 1, a_deg: 90, b_deg: 0, origin: [0, 0, 0] }`, then the same with `a_deg` -90. I do not know which pose was in progress when I stopped the process.\n- Then `GenerateOperation` for each pose.\n\n## Readings\n\n- With the seed `optimal_load`, the three poses took about 170 s in total (debug, `--test-threads=6`, other builds on the machine).\n- With `optimal_load` 0.5, the test process used one CPU core for more than 9 minutes. I stopped it. No result and no error came out.\n- Release: not tested.\n\n## Done means\n\n- A measurement in release and in debug tells if this is a hang or a slow path.\n- If it is a hang: the generator ends, or it refuses the op by name. A test pins it.\n- If it is only slow: record the reading here and close it, or file the speed work at the correct priority.\n",
